[0mThe provided material doesn't contain a dedicated ablation study section, but it does report several additional experiments that vary specific factors.

**1. Different LLM backends (MetaGPT on SoftwareDev, 5 tasks)**

| Backend | Open source | Time (s) | # Lines | Executability | Revisions |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| GPT-3.5 | No | 75.18 | 161.6 | 2.8 | 2.4 |
| GPT-4 | No | 552.94 | 178.2 | 3.8 | 1.2 |
| Deepseek Coder 33B | Yes | 1186.20 | 120.2 | 1.4 | 2.6 |

MetaGPT can complete tasks with all three backends, but GPT-4 gives the best results. It has the highest executability (3.8) and the fewest revisions (1.2). GPT-3.5 is the fastest. Deepseek Coder 33B is the slowest and has the lowest executability.

**2. Instruction level (high-level vs. detailed prompts, 5 tasks)**

| Prompt | # Words | Time (s) | Token usage | # Lines | Executability | Productivity | Revisions |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| High-level | 13.2 | 552.9 | 28,384.2 | 178.2 | 3.8 | 163.8 | 1.2 |
| Detailed | 42.2 | 567.8 | 29,657.0 | 257.0 | 4.0 | 118.0 | 1.6 |

Productivity is token usage divided by total code lines, so lower is better. Detailed prompts produce better software, with higher executability (4.0 vs. 3.8) and a lower productivity ratio (118.0 vs. 163.8), because the requirements and functions are clearer. Simple high-level prompts still produce good software, with an executability of 3.8 that is comparable to the detailed case.

**3. Executability comparison with other frameworks**

MetaGPT averaged 3.9 on a 1–4 scale. ChatDev averaged 2.1, and AutoGPT, LangChain and AgentVerse each scored 1.0. The generated code from these three baselines was often short, lacked comprehensive logic, and failed to handle cross-file dependencies. MetaGPT's advantage is attributed to its division of labor, its SOP workflow, and its structured messaging and feedback mechanisms.

**4. Executable feedback**

The context mentions a basic version of MetaGPT without the executable feedback mechanism, evaluated with GPT-4 32K on SoftwareDev tasks. On HumanEval and MBPP, the version without feedback scores 81.7% and 82.3%. The full MetaGPT scores 85.9% on HumanEval and 87.7% on MBPP, which suggests the feedback mechanism adds a few points. GPT-4 alone scores 67.0% on HumanEval.

**5. GPT variants on HumanEval**

GPT-4 and GPT-3.5-Turbo were also tested under several conditions, five runs each: calling the API directly, parsing the code with regex, and adding a system prompt that requests Python-only output. The details of these results are not included in the provided material.
